    "teach_8": {
      "id": "teach_8",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Capstone: symbolic chain rule strips away the story.\n\nIf x workers, x hours/day, for x days produce x units, then the rate constant k satisfies x = kx³, so k = 1/x².",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_8_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_8_step": {
      "id": "teach_8_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "With y workers, y hours/day and y days, output = (1/x²)·y³ = y³/x².\n\nThis is the same work-budget model, just written algebraically.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_8"
        }
      ]
    },
